<text><body><div type="page" n="121"><pb n="121" facs="#f0133"/>
<fw type="header" place="top">2. Wohnliche Einrichtung.</fw>
<table xml:id="p121-b1" facs="#f0133-b1" rows="30" cols="3"><row><cell>Slav. Wurzel.</cell><cell>Bedeutung.</cell><cell>Localnamen.</cell></row><row><cell>gora, hora</cell><cell>Berg</cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-gera">Gera</placeName>, <placeName ref="#place-gorlitzsch">Gorlitzsch</placeName>, <placeName ref="#place-goerkwitz">Görkwitz</placeName>, <placeName ref="#place-goeritz">Göritz</placeName>, <name type="nature" ref="#nature-goerlitz-huehnerbach">Görlitz</name>, <placeName ref="#place-harra">Harra</placeName>, <placeName ref="#place-horla">Horla</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>kholm</cell><cell>Berg</cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-kulm">Kulm</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>gama</cell><cell>Sattel</cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-gahma">Gahma</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>dele, djel, dole</cell><cell>Tiefe</cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-doehlen">Döhlen</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>pla, plawa</cell><cell>flach, glatt, eben</cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-poellwitz">Pöllwitz</placeName>, <placeName ref="#place-plauen">Plauen</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>bjel</cell><cell>flach, glatt, eben</cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-beulwitz">Beulwitz</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>mjel</cell><cell>flach, glatt, eben</cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-mielesdorf">Mielesdorf</placeName>, <placeName ref="#place-muehlsdorf">Mühlsdorf</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>roven</cell><cell>flach, glatt, eben</cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-roben">Roben</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>las, les</cell><cell>waldig</cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-laasen">Laasen</placeName>, <placeName ref="#place-laasen">Lossen</placeName>, <placeName ref="#place-loessau">Lössau</placeName>, <placeName ref="#place-doerflas">Dörflas</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>labe, loibe</cell><cell>waldig</cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-hohenleuben">Leube</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>bor</cell><cell>waldig</cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-poermitz">Pörmitz</placeName>, <placeName ref="#place-poersdorf">Pörsdorf</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>drewo</cell><cell>waldig</cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-trebnitz">Trebnitz</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>treb</cell><cell>steinig</cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-triebes">Triebes</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>trebona</cell><cell>Steinbach</cell><cell><name type="nature" ref="#nature-triebes">Triebes</name>.</cell></row><row><cell>lomniča</cell><cell>Wildwasser</cell><cell><name type="nature" ref="#nature-lemnitz">Lemnitz</name>.</cell></row><row><cell>leum</cell><cell>Quelle, Spring</cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-leumnitz">Leumnitz</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>pot</cell><cell>Quelle</cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-zoppothen">Zoppothen</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>pořiči</cell><cell>am Flusse</cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-poeritzsch">Pöritzsch</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>moz</cell><cell>feuchter Boden</cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-moeschlitz">Muschlitz</placeName>, <placeName ref="#place-moeschlitz">Möschlitz</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>lus</cell><cell>Sumpf</cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-lusan">Lusan</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>bano</cell><cell>Sumpf</cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-pahnstangen">Bahnstangen</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>gleino</cell><cell><rs type="concept" ref="#concept-lehm">Lehm</rs></cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-gleina">Gleina</placeName> *).</cell></row><row><cell>reja</cell><cell>reuten</cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-raila">Rayla</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>grob</cell><cell><name type="organism" ref="#organism-weissbuche">Weissbuche</name></cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-grobsdorf">Grobsdorf</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>topolina</cell><cell><name type="organism" ref="#organism-pappel">Pappel</name></cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-toeppeln">Töppeln</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>leube</cell><cell>Busch</cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-hohenleuben">Hohenleuben</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>ülsa, vülsa, wilscha</cell><cell><name type="organism" ref="#organism-erle">Erle</name></cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-wolschendorf">Wolschendorf</placeName>, Oelsch, <placeName ref="#place-elsch">Elsch</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>kot</cell><cell><name type="organism" ref="#organism-katze">Katze</name></cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-kattenstein">Kattenstein</placeName>.</cell></row><row><cell>kostriza</cell><cell><rs type="concept" ref="#concept-kirche">Kirche</rs></cell><cell><placeName ref="#place-koestritz">Köstritz</placeName>.</cell></row></table>
<p xml:id="p121-b2"><lb n="44" facs="#f0133-l44"/>Außerdem will man in den Benennungen <placeName ref="#place-schleiz">Schleiz</placeName> (<placeName ref="#place-schleiz">Slowitz</placeName>), Schwarm *<note place="foot" n="*)" xml:id="p121-fn1" facs="#f0133-fn1"><lb n="56" facs="#f0133-l56"/>Auch <placeName ref="#place-lueneburg">Lüneburg</placeName> hieß bei dem polabischen Stamme Glein.</note> <lb n="45" facs="#f0133-l45"/>bei <placeName ref="#place-untermhaus">Untermhaus</placeName>, <name type="nature" ref="#nature-sormitz">Sormitz</name> und <name type="nature" ref="#nature-sorbenbach">Sormbach</name> bei <placeName ref="#place-weitisberga">Weitisberga</placeName> selbst den Volks<lb n="46" break="no" facs="#f0133-l46"/>namen Slaven und Sorben finden, ebenso in <placeName ref="#place-boehmsdorf">Böhmsdorf</placeName> den der Böhmen.</p>
<p xml:id="p121-b3"><lb n="47" facs="#f0133-l47"/>Auf etwas festerem Grunde der Erklärung steht man bezüglich der deutschen <lb n="48" facs="#f0133-l48"/>Ortsnamen, obschon auch hier viele, namentlich die älteren, sich der sicheren <lb n="49" facs="#f0133-l49"/>Lösung entziehen. Das sorbische Idiom hat übrigens bewirkt, dass manche <lb n="50" facs="#f0133-l50"/>deutsche Namen durch starke Zusammenziehung einen harten, fast slavischen Klang <lb n="51" facs="#f0133-l51"/>angenommen haben. So Wolscht (= <placeName ref="#place-wolstieg">Wollstädt</placeName>), Gerauschts, Liebsch, Fitz'g. <lb n="52" facs="#f0133-l52"/>Unter den Ortsnamen endigen gegenwärtig *<note place="foot" n="**)" xml:id="p121-fn2" facs="#f0133-fn2"><lb n="57" facs="#f0133-l57"/>In den Theilungsacten von 1647 heißt es bei <placeName ref="#place-gera">Gera</placeName>: Das Haingut, das aus einer <lb n="58" facs="#f0133-l58"/><rs type="concept" ref="#concept-wiese">Wiese</rs> besteht und Schwarm heißt, ist ein Kammergut gewesen. Der alte Name Schwarm <lb n="59" facs="#f0133-l59"/>ist nicht ohne Bedeutung.</note> 40 auf dorf, wovon indes ein <lb n="53" facs="#f0133-l53"/>Theil slavisch-deutsch ist; die übrigen haben in kleinerer Zahl zu Endwörtern <lb n="54" facs="#f0133-l54"/>au (a), acker, bach, berg, brücken, brunn (born), burg, feld, grün, haus, hügel, <lb n="55" facs="#f0133-l55"/>mühle, reuth, stein und thal. Während die sorbischen Ortsnamen meist aus dem</p>
<p><note place="foot" n="***)" xml:id="p121-fn3" facs="#f0133-fn3"><lb n="60" facs="#f0133-l60"/>Früher noch 11 wüste Dörfer auf dorf endigend.</note></p>
</div></body></text>
